title: Analytics › Length of stay and units
route: /analytics
intro: Days or units asked for against days or units approved, by payer and by level of care. It sits in a folded section under 'Detailed breakdowns'. A cut is an approval for less than was asked, so denied requests are not in the averages.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Under 'Detailed breakdowns', click 'Length of stay and units'\nOr Tab to it and press Enter or Space"
screen sc "Closed: one summary line, for example 'Cardinal approves 90% of the days or units it is asked for, the lowest of the payers in view. 58 of its approvals were cut.'\nOpen: tabs 'All', 'Residential 3.5', 'IOP', 'PHP', 'Detox'"
click t1 "Click 'All'"
screen a1 "One bar for each payer: the share of the requested days or units that were approved\nRed under 80%\nThe line under the name: 'N approvals · N cut'"
click t2 "Click a level of care, for example 'Residential 3.5'"
screen a2 "Two bars for each payer: average days requested (grey) and approved (green)\nIOP counts units, the others days"
click c1 "Click a payer row"
process p1 "Opens the case list panel: 'Cardinal Health Plan: days and units requested and approved, Residential 3.5'\nDecisions that approved something, as requested or in part"
goto g1 "Continues in: Analytics › Case list panel"
click d1 "Click 'View data table'"
screen d2 "Payer, approvals, cut, requested and approved averages, share approved"
decision q1 "Any approvals in view?"
screen n1 "'No approvals in this view.'"
end e1 "Section read"

s1 --> sc --> t1 --> a1
sc --> t2 --> a2
a1 & a2 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| c1 --> p1 --> g1
q1 -->|No| n1 --> e1
a1 --> d1 --> d2
